Formbröd is a video editor for AmigaOS 4.

DESCRIPTION
Formbröd cuts, trims and joins video files, sound files and pictures on a
timeline, with fades, crossfades and effect modules, and exports the result
as a movie file. Video is read and written with the ffmpeg libraries, which
are built into the program.

Features:
- Tracks for video, sound and pictures, with film strip thumbnails and
  waveforms
- Trim, split and move clips by dragging, or by typing times
- Fades, crossfades (fade, wipes, slides, circle...) and per-clip volume
- Clips of any size and frame rate, fitted to the project's frame
- Preview with sound, rendered from small copies made in the background
- Save frames as IFF or PNG and export ranges as IFF ANIM, for drawing on
  in paint programs
- Projects saved as plain text
- ARexx port with every editing command
- English and Swedish

USAGE
Unpack the archive, open the Formbrod drawer and run Install-Formbrod. Or
just drag the drawer wherever you like.

Click Add file, trim with I and O at the playhead, play with Space, and
click Export. Formbrod.guide explains the rest, including ARexx:

  /* Join two files and export */
  ADDRESS FORMBROD
  'OPEN "Work:Video/intro.mp4"'
  'APPEND' RESULT '"Work:Video/main.mp4"'
  'EXPORT "Work:Video/final.mp4"'

CHANGES
1.1 - First release

REQUIREMENTS
AmigaOS 4.1 and AHI.

